Dutch rider Demi Vollering's late attack and solo break for victory earned the overall lead of the Women's Tour de France on Saturday as overnight leader Poland's Katarzyna Niewiadoma-Phinney finished third behind Italy's Elisa Longo Borghini.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6068019c-934f-11f1-8786-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Demi-Vollering-celebrates-her-8th-stage-win-of-Tour-de-France-Femmes-in-Nice-8-August-2026AFP-Nicolas-Tucat.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6068019c-934f-11f1-8786-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Demi-Vollering-celebrates-her-8th-stage-win-of-Tour-de-France-Femmes-in-Nice-8-August-2026AFP-Nicolas-Tucat.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7f349c6-9347-11f1-a5d3-9fca8092c76f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 18:53:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6068019c-934f-11f1-8786-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Demi-Vollering-celebrates-her-8th-stage-win-of-Tour-de-France-Femmes-in-Nice-8-August-2026AFP-Nicolas-Tucat.jpg">AFP - NICOLAS TUCAT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Think this summer is hot? El Nino could push temperatures even higher</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/think-this-summer-is-hot-el-nino-could-push-temperatures-even-higher-climate-change</link><description>
Record ocean heat, intensifying El Nino conditions and worsening extremes are raising the prospect that 2026 could become the hottest year ever measured.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05489a30-8fce-11f1-90fa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T050053Z-269844662-RC2BPMATL017-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-INSURANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05489a30-8fce-11f1-90fa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T050053Z-269844662-RC2BPMATL017-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-INSURANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d33458f0-918e-11f1-9d67-e135b2d0c4c5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 13:16:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/05489a30-8fce-11f1-90fa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T050053Z-269844662-RC2BPMATL017-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-INSURANCE.jpg">© REUTERS - Manon Cruz </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers bracing for smallest corn harvest in 40 years</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260808-french-farmers-bracing-for-smallest-corn-harvest-in-40-years-drought-heatwave-environment</link><description>
France's corn harvest is on pace this year for a 35 percent fall to nine million tons, a level last seen in 1980 for Europe's biggest grains producer, the government said Friday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e60c450c-1623-11ea-bbbd-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/6f15c24231593979539fd1689d0e9297f6795cac.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e60c450c-1623-11ea-bbbd-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/6f15c24231593979539fd1689d0e9297f6795cac.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc081f96-9336-11f1-997c-f5115488d840</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 14:44:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e60c450c-1623-11ea-bbbd-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/6f15c24231593979539fd1689d0e9297f6795cac.jpg">AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Former French PM Attal files legal complaint over alleged Russian interference</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260808-former-french-pm-attal-files-legal-complaint-over-alleged-russian-interference</link><description>
Former French prime minitser Gabriel Attal, also a candidate in the 2027 presidential election, has filed a legal complaint alleging "foreign interference originating from Russian networks" after discovering he was the target of several deepfakes, fake news videos and fake newspaper front pages earlier this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65635316-25a2-11f0-80ee-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T140948Z_954268298_RC299Y97ALTY_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-RUSSIA-CYBERSECURITY.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65635316-25a2-11f0-80ee-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T140948Z_954268298_RC299Y97ALTY_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-RUSSIA-CYBERSECURITY.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6693d2e-930b-11f1-b6de-6109cceefb43</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 09:46:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/65635316-25a2-11f0-80ee-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T140948Z_954268298_RC299Y97ALTY_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-RUSSIA-CYBERSECURITY.JPG">REUTERS - Dado Ruvic</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>High stakes for Ireland's EU presidency amid migration row over Ceuta crisis</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260808-high-stakes-for-ireland-s-eu-presidency-amid-migration-row-over-ceuta-crisis</link><description>
Ireland this week found itself at the centre of Europe’s increasingly fraught migration debate, as it sought to calm a dispute among European Union member states following last week's influx of 50,000 people into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ba6c5f4-9187-11f1-8912-fd507ef24b37</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 07:34:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg">© AFP/Ben Stansall</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey's new opposition party offers hope, but its future is already in jeopardy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260808-turkey-s-new-opposition-party-offers-hope-but-its-future-is-already-in-jeopardy</link><description>
The launch of the Yeni Party in Turkey promises to energise the country's struggling opposition. But while some polls show it leading, it remains vulnerable – already beset by arrests it says are "politically motivated". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4b81e0c8-5eab-11f1-affd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/TURQUIE-OZGUR-OZEL-PARLEMENT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4b81e0c8-5eab-11f1-affd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/TURQUIE-OZGUR-OZEL-PARLEMENT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4d9894a-9230-11f1-9dba-e3260db61049</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 10:20:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ivorian drum, looted by France, goes on display for first time at home</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260808-ivorian-drum-looted-by-france-goes-on-display-for-first-time-djidji-ayokwe</link><description>
The Djidji Ayokwe, a sacred "talking drum" which was looted by French colonial troops in 1916 and taken to France, arrived in its home village in Côte d'Ivoire on Friday, where local people were able to see it for the first time since it was repatriated in March. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5410b5fe-9315-11f1-83b6-5f422980672c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 10:52:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bc3fc75c-381e-11f1-acc7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98CW9TK.jpg">AFP - BERTRAND GUAY</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Niewiadoma-Phinney seizes Tour de France Femmes lead on Mont Ventoux</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260808-niewiadoma-phinney-seizes-tour-de-france-femmes-lead-on-mont-ventoux</link><description>
Poland's Katarzyna Niewiadoma-Phinney sprung a surprise on her two rivals Marlen Reusser and Demi Vollering with a long-range solo win at Mont Ventoux during the Women's Tour de France Queen stage on Friday, edging her into a narrow overall lead.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f84c89d0-9276-11f1-99d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-31.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f84c89d0-9276-11f1-99d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-31.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d49b2bc-9302-11f1-b3d5-27c203c3191e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 08:31:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f84c89d0-9276-11f1-99d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/image1-31.jpeg">© Pierre René-Worms / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>The EU has new anti-Beijing instruments, but will China have to face the music?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260807-the-eu-has-new-anti-beijing-instruments-but-will-china-have-to-face-the-music</link><description>
When Western companies rushed into China in the 1980s and 1990s, they traded their latest technology for market access. Now, China has absorbed, adapted and improved foreign know-how and is flooding Europe with advanced products, while the European Union's trade deficit balloons. As Paris and Berlin finally align on a response, analysts question whether Brussels' defensive "instruments" can contain a rival it helped create.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a422fd2-9172-11f1-a419-8d27d6502f9b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 20:05:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Rwanda in talks with Italy to take in migrants trying to reach EU</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260807-rwanda-in-talks-with-italy-to-take-in-migrants-trying-to-reach-eu</link><description>
Days after Italy proposed setting up a network of migrant reception centres outside the European Union, Rwanda has confirmed that it is in talks with the Italian government about potentially hosting people seeking asylum in the EU.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa626000-9244-11f1-8c80-c9b100b5e473</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:01:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Pope Leo XIV to meet survivors of clerical abuse during September visit to France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260807-pope-leo-xiv-to-meet-abuse-survivors-during-september-visit-to-france</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV will meet privately with survivors of clerical sexual abuse during a four-day visit to France next month. On Friday, the Vatican published the itinerary for the 25–28 September trip – the first papal state visit to the country since Benedict XVI visited in 2008.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">065720b0-925b-11f1-98cd-15ecfd29aa41</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 13:31:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg">AFP - HANDOUT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo hands first prisoners back to M23 rebels under peace deal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260807-dr-congo-hands-first-prisoners-back-to-m23-rebels-under-peace-deal</link><description>
